# RoleCall .gitignore
# Note: .gitignore does not support trailing inline comments (a "#" after a
# pattern is treated as part of the pattern), so each rule's explanation sits
# on its own line directly above it.

# ── Personal / local Claude config ─────────────────────────────
# Your private, machine-specific notes for Claude Code. CLAUDE.md (shared build
# rules) IS committed; this local variant is personal, so keep it out of git.
CLAUDE.local.md

# ── Secrets & environment variables ────────────────────────────
# Real secrets: API keys, database URLs, auth tokens. Must never reach GitHub.
.env
# Environment-specific variants (.env.local, .env.production, etc.) — same risk.
.env.*
# But DO keep a committed template of which vars are needed (values left blank),
# so the exception below re-includes it.
!.env.example
# Private keys / TLS certificates — credentials, never belong in a repo.
*.pem
*.key

# ── Real job-search data (privacy) ─────────────────────────────
# Your actual applications contain personal info. Seed the app's database at
# runtime instead; anything you mark ".local" or ".private" stays off GitHub.
*.local.json
*.private.json
seed.local.*

# ── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Installed packages: huge, and fully regenerated by `npm install`. Never commit.
node_modules/

# ── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production build artifacts — generated from source, not source themselves.
dist/
build/
# Vite's dev cache — generated and machine-local.
.vite/

# ── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log files: noise, machine-specific, not part of the source.
*.log
# npm's crash logs, written only on failures — not needed in git.
npm-debug.log*

# ── OS / editor cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS Finder metadata — junk on any other machine.
.DS_Store
# Windows thumbnail cache — Windows-generated junk.
Thumbs.db
# VS Code workspace settings — personal IDE prefs, not project source.
.vscode/
# JetBrains IDE settings — same reason.
.idea/
